id: pm-zclzll
title: "Mutation-testing gate: prove the 100 percent coverage suite actually detects defects, with a ratcheted mutation score on SDK core"
description: "Add mutation testing for the SDK core so nominal 100 percent coverage is proven to detect behavioral defects, with a ratcheted score and explicit survivor ownership."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: "area:sdk",ci,defect-detection,mutation-testing,quality-gate,testing
created_at: "2026-07-24T23:46:02.748Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-22T14:32:05.636Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-22T14:32:04.448Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-22T14:32:04.448Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 1200
acceptance_criteria: "A mutation-testing run produces a reproducible score for the SDK core module set in CI; The score is ratcheted: regressions fail, improvements move the floor, matching the existing suppressions-ratchet discipline; Runtime is bounded — incremental or partitioned execution keeps the gate inside the nightly budget rather than the pull-request budget if necessary; Surviving mutants are triaged with either a new assertion or a written equivalent-mutant waiver; no blanket ignores"
goal: ci-detects-every-defect
objective: Coverage stops being a proxy for test strength and becomes a measured property
value: "Literal 100 percent all-source coverage is enforced, but coverage only proves lines executed — it cannot distinguish an assertion from a bare call. Mutation score measures what coverage claims."
impact: "Closes the largest blind spot in the quality gates: a suite can be fully green, fully covering, and still miss an entire class of introduced defects."
outcome: "A mutation score baseline exists for the SDK core with a ratchet that fails CI on regression, and surviving mutants are triaged into either new assertions or recorded equivalent-mutant waivers."
why_now: "The coverage ADR settled the coverage question; the next honest question is assertion strength, and it is cheapest to baseline before the SDK promotion partition finishes moving code."
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "Added sandboxed complete mutation execution, exact owned equivalent-mutant triage, source/report validation, a monotonic score and scope floor, required static/nightly/release integration, retained CI evidence, and stronger existing SDK behavioral assertions"
expected_result: "The declared SDK partition detects behavioral changes and rejects unowned survivors, stale evidence, scope/floor regression, skipped mutants and unsafe execution overrides within a bounded runtime"
actual_result: "330 mutants executed: 323 killed and seven justified equivalents at 97.87878787878788 percent; linked built and prebuilt runs passed, exact all-source coverage is 100/100/100/100, and isolated retries resolved two local load-related test timeouts. Local import/transport timing remains over budget and must pass unchanged on hosted CI before merge"
