comments[13]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-22T13:27:10.205Z","harness:codex","All-status orientation recovered 2795 complete item records and 67658 full history events without omissions. Canonical mutation-testing owner reused alongside pm-dvwm for a connected test/documentation-quality tranche. GitHub has no open PRs or dependency, code-scanning, or secret-scanning alerts; issue 1246 already links its canonical onboarding owner. No unrelated item claimed."
  "2026-09-22T13:40:46.625Z","harness:codex","Mutation-driven assertions raised the measured partition from 275/330 killed after correct existing-test selection to 322/330 killed (97.57575757575758 percent). Eight remaining mutations are behaviorally equivalent and individually explained by exact identity, source, replacement, and owner. No mutants excluded. Focused 75-test run passes; dependency audit has zero vulnerabilities. Full all-source coverage and hosted verification remain pending."
  "2026-09-22T13:48:49.095Z","harness:codex",Graph verification caught the newly added generic related edge exceeding the no-growth ceiling. Removing that incidental co-delivery edge; existing implements and verifies lineage already explains this gate without inventing a semantic dependency on documentation cleanup.
  "2026-09-22T13:49:08.000Z","harness:codex","Independent acceptance passed 18 commands each under Node 26.9.0 and Bun in external temporary project/global trackers: init, hierarchical typed create, claim/update, comments/notes/learnings, get/list/search/context, graph ancestors, atomic close/release, strict history verification, and resolution/history validation. Production Sentry/required telemetry gate passed: zero critical/high issues, 2.05 percent error rate, zero failures lacking error codes. Registry audit reports no vulnerabilities. Evidence logs remain ignored locally."
  "2026-09-22T13:50:56.819Z","harness:codex","The graph gate also preserves prose-to-edge completeness. Retained the factual co-delivery cross-reference and refined the older generic link to the quality epic into implements: this task now delivers the epic's local quality parity and regression prevention gate. Related-edge total stays at the existing ceiling without inventing a dependency between the two gates."
  "2026-09-22T13:59:46.192Z","harness:codex","Full-suite first pass: 9221 tests passed and two release-contract assertions correctly rejected the old static command expectation. Updated their shared expected contract to require both new gates. No coverage report was produced on that failed test pass, so no 100 percent claim is made. Packed npm/npx/bunx package smoke passed; concurrent package dogfood timed out waiting for the long coverage lease and will be rerun after contention clears."
  "2026-09-22T14:02:51.437Z","harness:codex","Release command contracts now pass, and the three new gate modules have exact focused coverage of 142/142 statements, 107/107 branches, 21/21 functions, and 105/105 lines. New negative controls cover attached parameter tags and attempts to introduce filler budgets for previously clean files. Package-first dogfood passed on the uncontended rerun. Full all-source coverage remains a separate pending rerun."
  "2026-09-22T14:05:33.776Z","harness:codex",The repository static gate rejected the expanded sandbox runner at complexity 19 against the mandatory ceiling 16. Separated validation-stage dispatch from temporary-root/build lifecycle without changing process or cleanup ordering; both functions now satisfy the original ceiling. No suppression or budget increase introduced.
  "2026-09-22T14:17:36.214Z","harness:codex","All-source exact coverage passed with zero uncovered counts: 65025/65025 statements, 49627/49627 branches, 13494/13494 functions, 62184/62184 lines. The six-worker run passed 9223 tests but timed out two existing executable gates (refusal closure and scale benchmark), which passed in the earlier four-worker run. Those tests are rerunning alone with original timeouts; full coverage is not being conflated with an all-green test run."
  "2026-09-22T14:20:16.006Z","harness:codex","Survivor review correction: a direct runtime experiment disproved the proposed Date.parse trim equivalence. Whitespace-padded ISO timestamps can parse to NaN without trim, so that waiver was invalid. Removed it, changed the existing provider timestamp assertion to a padded ISO timestamp with a deterministic fallback clock, and raised the expected floor to 323/330. This is a real assertion-strength gap, not an equivalent mutant. Actual mutation rerun is required before accepting the new score."
  "2026-09-22T14:22:40.799Z","harness:codex","Final targeted rerun passed all 17 tests across refusal-closure and scale-benchmark suites at their original timeouts. The real prebuilt mutation run passed in 42 seconds: 330 total, 323 killed, seven exact equivalents, zero uncovered/timeout/error mutants, score 97.87878787878788. Date trimming is now asserted rather than waived. Full all-source exact coverage remains 100/100/100/100; no source behavior, coverage exclusion or timeout budget was weakened."
  "2026-09-22T14:30:18.682Z","harness:codex","Static verification passed repository quality, exact docstring coverage, zero duplication, package/SDK boundaries, grammar/flags, refusal closure, token budgets, tracker context, gate registry and surface freshness. The local Node 26.9 import-cost gate remains slightly over budget (core 430/423 ms, governance 329/327 ms, merge 239/226 ms) on isolated retry. Executable TypeScript AST comparison proves both touched SDK files are unchanged from main. Budgets remain unchanged; checking the CI Node 24 runtime and remaining independent gates before hosted verification."
  "2026-09-22T14:32:01.531Z","harness:codex","Local performance limitation retained: import and CLI transport timing budgets still fail on this workstation, including a Node 24 probe. No budget was raised, no passing sample was selected, and no blanket green static claim is made. The touched SDK executable ASTs are unchanged; hosted Node 24 timing gates remain mandatory before merge. All functional retries, exact four-metric source coverage, mutation partition, dependency/security inventories, package acceptance, typecheck and documentation coverage have passed."
notes[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T07:13:38.584Z","harness:claude-code","Coverage-pragma density measured 2026-07-25, relevant to whether the 100% literal all-src number proves defect detection. 465 v8/c8/istanbul ignore pragmas exist across src, scripts and packages against the static-quality-gate ceiling MAX_COVERAGE_IGNORE_PRAGMAS = 496, i.e. 94% of the budget is consumed. They concentrate in exactly the largest and most complex files: src/sdk/governance/validate.ts 65, src/cli/main.ts 51, src/cli/commands/create.ts 37, src/sdk/governance/health.ts 25, src/sdk/extension.ts 24, src/sdk/test/execution.ts 22, src/cli/commands/contracts.ts 22, src/sdk/query/search.ts 21, src/sdk/history-redact.ts 21. vitest.config.ts excludes only src/**/*.d.ts, so the 100% figure is genuine for everything not pragma-excluded — which makes the pragma set, not the config, the real coverage boundary. A mutation score computed over SDK core should treat these regions explicitly: they are the places where surviving mutants are most likely and least visible. The ceiling is also a ceiling only, not a ratchet, so the count can grow to 496 without any gate reacting."
  "2026-09-22T13:42:38.171Z","harness:codex","Engine configuration is development-only Stryker 10.0.0 with the installed Vitest 4.1.11 adapter. Initial partition uses two SDK correctness boundaries and all mutants, with no ignore directives or mutator exclusions. Full SDK mutation expansion is future work; all-source coverage remains mandatory independently."
  "2026-09-22T14:11:16.717Z","harness:codex","Execution controls override the declarative engine configuration: in-place mutation, incremental reuse, static-mutant skipping, external configuration loading, and blanket excluded mutation operators are disabled. Unit controls deliberately supply those unsafe settings and verify the effective engine options; the required real mutation run independently measures actual assertion strength."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-22T13:42:39.613Z","harness:codex","A covered transport-refusal branch is not evidence that its lexical guard is asserted: Node Buffer accepts junk around base64url and JSON parsing can still succeed. Assert invalid-byte refusal independently from payload validation."
  "2026-09-22T14:20:18.529Z","harness:codex",Do not infer runtime equivalence from API familiarity. Date.parse accepts some padded legacy dates but rejects padded ISO timestamps; experimentally test waiver claims with the actual supported input family before retaining them.
